                <pb facs="0676" n="604" sameAs="frus:frus1865p4/pg604"/>

                <head>Polish Refugees of Zurich</head>
                <note rend="inline" rendition="#center" type="source">[Translation.]</note>
                <dateline>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bendlikon, near Zurich</hi></placeName>, <lb/>
                    <date calendar="gregorian" when="1865-05-02">
                        <hi rendition="#italic">May</hi> 2, 1865</date>.</dateline>
                <p>We, the emigrants from Poland, participate in the feeling of horror experienced
                    by all nations at the death of Mr. Lincoln, President of the United States, who
                    deserved well of humanity. Received with hospitality upon the soil of
                    Switzerland, we join our voices with the Helvetians in expressions of condolence
                    with the American people, and with their wishes that the country where Pulaski
                    and Kosciusko fought with Washington may be strengthened in its independence and
                    integrity by the absolute abolition of slavery, clemency towards the conquered,
                    equality of all its inhabitants, and respect for the liberty of other
                    nations.</p>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Managers and printers of the “Polish paper called the
                        Ojczyzna:</hi>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <list>
                            <item>AGATON GILLER, <hi rendition="#italic">Responsible
                                Editor</hi>.</item>
                            <item>RADOMIRISK.</item>
                            <item>ANTOINE SWIEREZEWSKI.</item>
                            <item>JOSEPH KOSSOBRUZKI.</item>
                            <item>THEODORE DZWIGATSKI.</item>
                            <item>JOSEPH HARASIMOWIOZ.</item>
                            <item>LEOPOLD BUCZON.</item>
                            <item>JULIUSZ MILEWSKI.</item>
                            <item>BOLESLAS KOWALEWSKI.</item>
                            <item>HEINRICH KAPPE.</item>
                            <item>HIPOLIT OBRYSKI.</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
